  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 305 PM EDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nWater vapor imagery and RAP analysis reveal deep upper level \ntroughing centered over Quebec this afternoon, with lingering cold \nair advection in northwest flow supporting some lake induced clouds \nand a few rain showers over the eastern half of the UP this \nafternoon. Meanwhile, surface high pressure is building in from the \nwest, making for clear skies across the rest of the area with \ntemperatures mainly in the 50s today. Showers will diminish through \nthe rest of the afternoon into this evening as high pressure \ncontinues to move across the region.\n\nAttention then quickly turns to another low dropping out of central \nCanada into Ontario on Tuesday. A weak warm air advection regime \nahead of this system will bring the chance for some light overrunning \nprecipitation across the UP tonight into Tuesday. Any rain that does \nmanage to reach the ground will be limited to a trace to a few \nhundredths of an inch given weak forcing and dry antecedent \nconditions. Also can't rule out the potential for a few snowflakes \nto mix in overnight as some interior locations dip into the low to \nmid 30s. Look for showers to potentially increase in coverage later \nin the day across the east as better forcing arrives with the \nprogression of the upper trough into Ontario. Temperatures will run \nas much as 10-15 degrees higher than today on Tuesday afternoon as \nsoutherly low level flow sends highs into the upper 60s in the north \nand the low 70s in the south. This will be accompanied by gusty \nsouth winds aided by a 40 kt low level jet, producing 15 to 25 mph \nwinds gusts across much of the area and some 30+ mph gusts along the \nLake Superior shoreline.  \n\nCold air advection quickly returns Tuesday night into Wednesday in \nthe wake of the system, kicking off another round of potential lake \neffect rain showers and breezy conditions during the middle to later \nportion of the week as temperatures return to seasonal norms in the \n50s for Thursday and Friday. Surface ridging then favors drier and \nwarmer weather into the weekend.",
